{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-11T05:32:47.385Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e6ba0f6f7044b066fe23d5ec","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4yxzvd","claim:pm-gh1700","claim:pm-pwqiao","claim:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-4yxzvd+pm-gh1700+pm-pwqiao+pm-tuxw1i","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-4yxzvd","claim:pm-gh1700","claim:pm-pwqiao","claim:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-tuxw1i","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-11T05:32:47.385Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-11T05:32:47.384Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Design on branch fix/collection-mutation-receipts (2026-11-11).\n\n1. Scoped scalar clear. A shared predicate, scalarClearRemovesDependency in src/sdk/lifecycle/start-blockers.ts, decides which rows a scalar clear removes. update.ts uses it for the write, and the start refusal uses it to decide whether to advertise --unset blocked_by. The scalar clear (--unset blocked_by, or --blocked-by none) removes a literal blocked_by row in two cases:\n   - its stored id is the scalar's own text, from any source;\n   - its stored id is the scalar's canonical id (normalizeItemId), and its source_kind is cli:create:blocked_by or cli:update:blocked_by, the rows a --blocked-by write derives.\n\n   The provenance condition keeps the existing conservative case. A short scalar 'a' beside a hand-added 'pm-a' row (via --dep) may name two distinct items, because locateItem resolves exact-first while the --blocked-by set path resolves canonical-first. The clear therefore keeps that row.\n\n2. Explicit kind-wide removal. --dep-remove kind=<kind> with no other key removes every row of that kind; this is AC 2's separately named operation. Zero matches give the usual dependency_remove_no_match refusal, with unmatched_selectors id '*' so the public PmCliErrorContext type keeps a string id. An id-less selector carrying any other key is still refused rather than widened.\n\n3. Removal receipt. mutateUpdateDocument diffs the stored rows before and after, as a multiset keyed by full stored identity. It emits dependencies_removed:<item>:<id>/<kind>,... whenever rows were removed by any path: scalar clear, --dep-remove, --clear-deps or --replace-deps. The flat CLI receipt and the SDK result both carry warnings.\n\n4. Recovery producers re-checked. Three places advertise --unset blocked_by:\n   - start-blockers now advertises it for multi-edge items (AC 4).\n   - The close.ts pending-unblock recovery becomes strictly safer, because a blocker added concurrently keeps its edge and validate reports it. The docs/COMMANDS.md sentence that claimed every edge is removed is corrected.\n   - The validate.ts dangling hint is unchanged: its source 'blocked_by' row is the scalar itself."}]}],"before_hash":"f8716ed0e1c1abf26248ecf9f7c40554cf3924261a4464fd4b04ddfcafe973f8","after_hash":"82e61bc4fbfc271ac0b5b3c8049649cdbb176e81d655538f03b94b1a6c0095cd","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0162cc27d020548c29dccaff299c5315c06ba79476422db07051d0972c259aa1"}
